   "Parts are unchanged from step 1; none added or dropped.",
   "Circuit image: the buzzer legs sit in columns 5 and 8 on the row-h side of the breadboard. The image shows rows f-j in the upper half, so these holes are named with bank 'b' (rows f-j) per the catalogue.",
   "The black wire goes from Uno GND (the header pin next to AREF, GND.1) to hole 5b.g. It shares a strip with the buzzer leg in 5b.h, so that leg is ground.",
   "The red wire goes from Uno pin 8 to hole 8b.g. It shares a strip with the buzzer leg in 8b.h, so that leg is the signal (+) leg. The schematic agrees: pin 8 to +, GND to -.",
   "The catalogue buzzer has ports 1 and 2 and does not say which is +. I assumed port 1 is + (to pin 8) and port 2 is - (to GND).",
   "No series resistor is used, matching the tutorial's parts list, circuit and schematic."
  ]
